DESCRIPTION:Meet with others to discuss books centering disability voices!
  Copies of each month's books are available at the Sonoma County Library C
 atalog. Pre-Register to receive a reminder email. Drop-ins are welcome. If
  you didn't have time to read or finish the month's book\, you are still w
 elcome to attend. Snacks will be provided. Common Ground Society serves fa
 milies who have loved ones with any sort of unique need while also educati
 ng our community on how to be inclusive. Held the 1st Friday of the month 
 from 10:30-11:30am. We will not be meeting in January. 09/4/2026- What My 
 Bones Know by Stephanie Foo- Meet at Ives Park 10/2/2026- The Cancer Journ
 als by Audre Lorde- Meet at Ives Park 11/06/2026- Hunchback by Saou Ichika
 wa- Meet at Ives Park 12/04/2026- Unmasking Autism by Devon Price 02/05/20
 27- Mother Tongue by Sara Nović 03/05/2027- I'm Telling the Truth\, but I
 'm Lying by Bassey Ikpi 04/02/2027- I'll Look So Hot in My Coffin by Carla
  Sosenko 05/07/2027- TBD
LOCATION:Common Ground Book Club: books by & about people with disabilitie
 s
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/common-ground-book-club-books-a
 bout-people-disabilities-122388
