BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday with Dawn & Tony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T200000
UID:261124Zig4fWrArk-1D2XIEkhrjg
DESCRIPTION:“Dawn Angelosante brings a keen pop sensibility and heartfel
 t passion to every performance. Her voice wraps her lyrics into a dreamsca
 pe of sound and story\, touching on love\, friendship\, heartbreak and sel
 f-reflection. Tony Gibson’s songwriting blends infectious melodies with 
 honest\, emotionally resonant lyrics. His music feels both familiar and fr
 esh\, painting vivid portraits of real-life moments.\n\nMichael Fecskes\, 
 a classically trained cellist and composer\, adds a unique depth to the gr
 oup’s sound. Drawing from his Hungarian and Caribbean roots\, his compos
 itions are rich and soulful\, and his experience as a performer and educat
 or brings both sensitivity and creativity to the ensemble.\n\nTogether\, D
 awn\, Tony and Michael form a dynamic singer-songwriter/folk/pop trio. Sin
 ce 2021 they’ve combined their individual voices and musical influences 
 into a lush\, intimate soundscape\, layering acoustics guitar\, piano\, an
 d cello\, with haunting vocal harmonies. Whether sharing original composit
 ions or fresh takes on covers\, they’ve captivated audiences throughout 
 Sonoma\, Napa and the North Bay with performances that are both personal a
 nd powerful."
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-1205202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T235900
UID:261124PLCur6oxCUOiIBxuTE2lzw
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
