DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
UID:261123s69AYwKi5UaC2ORY0vRhHg
DESCRIPTION:Jack’s Bookshop at Jack London State Historic Park will host
  a special “Deck the Shelves: Member Appreciation Day” on Saturday\, D
 ec. 5\, at 10 a.m. to 5 p.m.   Those with park memberships\, including t
 hose who become members that day\, will receive a 20% discount on all in-p
 erson purchases \\(membership and park entrance fees not included\\).  Th
 e first 40 members to visit and make a purchase will receive a complimenta
 ry branded tote bag.\n\nJack’s Bookshop\, inside the House of Happy Wall
 s Museum\, features museum-editions of the complete works of Jack London\,
  one of the most successful writers of the 20th century whose stories cont
 inue to engage readers of all ages around the world. His most famous novel
 \, “The Call of the Wild\,” for example\, is available in versions for
  ages 7 to adults.  \n\nJack's Bookshop also offers titles authored by Ch
 armian London\, his wife\, and various biographies that give insight into 
 their adventurous lives.  Jack’s Bookshop also carries apparel\, statio
 nery\, and souvenirs that make the perfect holiday gifts for nature and bo
 ok lovers alike. New t-shirts\, sweatshirts\, hats\, and tote bags are now
  available\, all made in collaboration with local screenprinting studio So
 noma Ink. \n\nAnnual memberships to the park make excellent gifts.  Star
 ting at $59\, membership includes a pass for entry to the park all year fo
 r the pass holder and up to nine passengers in a private vehicle.  The re
 gular entry fee is $15 per vehicle.  The annual membership pass is also v
 alid for entrance to Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, just eight miles away in
  Kenwood\, CA. \n\nBooks and other items can be ordered online at https:/
 /jacklondonpark.com/jacks-shop/all-items/ \\(the Dec. 15 discount does not
  apply to online orders\\). All purchases support the non-profit Jack Lond
 on Park Partners\, which funds and operates the park.  Passes can also be
  ordered online and will be mailed to the giver or the recipient.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/jacks-shop/all-items/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
