DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T160000
UID:2611186HgUrJc6ZkizL8hzV9EF3A
DESCRIPTION:A free community experience with voices from the past\, presen
 t\, and future\, followed by intergenerational party celebrating queer joy
 . Presented by the Russian River Historical Society. Main presentation\, 2
 -4pm Overview of the Russian River Historical Society's project to documen
 t and digitize historical material related to AIDS history in the Russian 
 River area and Sonoma County Highlights and voices from the project archiv
 es and oral history collection Future access through Sonoma County Library
 's Digital Archives Information about the Sonoma County Library's Here & Q
 ueer project. Intergenerational dance party\, 4-6pm In 2024\, the Russian 
 River Historical Society and Sonoma County Library collaborated on a joint
  grant project to digitize and describe LGBTQ\\+ material in the RRHS' arc
 hive related to AIDS. Learn more about the Russian River Historical Societ
 y's work to preserve queer local history.
LOCATION:Dawn Ranch
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/surviving-and-thriving-rivers-r
 esponse-aids-122658
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
