BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Swingles: Together For The Holidays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T190000
UID:2610208TSdSKnjhUS8Y3k8eGUQCw
DESCRIPTION:The Swingles have been challenging the boundaries of vocal mus
 ic for over 60 years\, earning 5 Grammy® Awards and establishing themselv
 es as one of the world’s most beloved and admired vocal groups.\n\nThrou
 ghout its various iterations \\(Les Swingles Singers / Swingle II / The Ne
 w Swingle Singers / The Swingles / The Swingle Singers \\(and since 2014\,
  The Swingles again\\)\\)\, the group's signature and instantly-recognisab
 le sound has remained constant and timeless and their intricate arrangemen
 ts remain unparalleled. The current singers are masters of their craft\, c
 onstantly seeking new ways of reimagining jazz\, folk\, pop and classical 
 music from their ever-growing repertoire\, alongside creating a rich vein 
 of new original material. Their combination of close-microphone amplificat
 ion paired with the extraordinary range and vocal dexterity of the group
 ’s seven individual voices to create one seamlessly-blended vocal sound\
 , has captured the admiration of composers and collaborators alike\, who h
 ave embraced the sheer versatility of the group and its genre-crossing pos
 sibilities.\n\nAmerican-born Ward Swingle first assembled a group of Paris
 ian session singers to sing through Bach’s Well-Tempered Clavier as a vo
 cal exercise in 1962. The resulting album ‘Jazz Sebastian Bach’ \\(rec
 orded initially for friends and family\\)\, became a huge hit\, breaking n
 ew musical ground and launching The Swingles to fame. Several of the singe
 rs had previously sung with Mimi Perrin’s group Les Double Six \\(who wi
 th Quincy Jones and Dizzy Gillespie recorded the 6 voices twice in order t
 o create a much larger sound and richer chord structure\\). The Swingles o
 f today employ a similar technique in their current shows - an immersive l
 ayering up of vocals using live-looping technology to record themselves in
  the moment and have it play back later\, producing mesmeric \\(and potent
 ially massive\\) musical textures.\n\nThe group has released more than 50 
 albums encompassing a huge range of music in many different styles\, fuell
 ed by Ward Swingle’s pioneering spirit and varied musical tastes. Their 
 arrangements tend either to give a little twist to the original or turn it
  completely on its head. The group’s genre-inclusive approach to music-m
 aking has led to collaborations with artists such as Jamie Cullum\, Gareth
  Malone\, Kurt Elling\, New York Voices\, and Labrinth. They co-wrote and 
 performed a song for the end credits of Alexander Payne’s film ‘Downsi
 zing’ and have appeared on many film and TV soundtracks\, including ‘G
 rey’s Anatomy’\, ‘Sex and the City’\, ‘Wedding Crashers’\, ‘
 The Holdovers’\, ‘The Two Popes’\, and ‘Glee’.\n\n"superhero sin
 ging to truly raise goosebumps.”\n\nTHE GUARDIAN\n\n"The Swingles were n
 ever less than dazzling”\n\nTHE WASHINGTON POST
LOCATION:Brannan Center
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1038490589?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BellyDancing with Carem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T190000
UID:261012VkRttNQKFkOga_778vi1ag
DESCRIPTION:Bellydancing for Beginners \n\nDiscover the beauty of Raqs Sh
 arqi \\(bellydance\\). This beginner-friendly class introduces you to fou
 ndational bellydance technique\, including hip movements\, isolations\, un
 dulations\, traveling steps\, combinations and musicality. You’ll develo
 p coordination\, body awareness\, strength\, and confidence while learning
  to move with greater ease and expression.\n\nNo previous dance experience
  is required. All bodies and experience levels are welcome.\n\nCome move t
 o the music\, connect with your body\, and discover the joy of bellydancin
 g\n\nCAREM LOVE\n\nCarem Love is a wellness advocate\, professional dancer
 \, and certified yoga instructor with a Bachelor’s degree in Dance. She 
 has extensive training in Bellydance\, a deep passion for Latin dance\, an
 d is certified in Hatha\, Vinyasa\, and Children’s Yoga.\n\nBelly dance 
 has profoundly supported her health\, well-being\, and dance career\, insp
 iring her to help others experience the same body-mind benefits. In her cl
 asses\, students learn to connect more deeply with themselves.\n\nDATE: Mo
 nday\n\nTIME: 6:00 PM\n\nWHERE: Salsa Dance Marin\, 4140 Redwood Hwy 8\, S
 an Rafael
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/belly-dancing-with-carem/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261207T170000
UID:260824WL3IalOyqUmR3CaZGbm0DA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
