BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Los Cien Holiday Party: Noche de Gratitud
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T200000
UID:26112552O_vQkSO0eOSG2WV4aHTw
DESCRIPTION:Los Cien Holiday Party &ndash\; Noche de Gratitud\n\nA communi
 ty-centered\, family-friendly celebration of Latine culture during the hol
 iday season.\n\nThe year is wrapping up\, and we're celebrating the way we
  know best: together. Our comunidad showed up again and again this year\, 
 and every program and gathering happened because of our volunteers\, membe
 rs\, staff\, partners\, and friends. Now it's our turn to say gracias.\n\n
 Come hang out with the Los Cien familia at Sally Tomatoes in Rohnert Park 
 for appetizers\, karaoke\, and a little friendly holiday competition.\n\nE
 vent Details:\n\nLocation: Sally Tomatoes\n\nAddress: 1100 Valley House Dr
 .\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nDate &amp\; Time: Thursday\, December 10 | 
 5:30pm to 8:00pm\n\nRSVP: Space is limited to the first 200 guests &ndash\
 ; reserve your spot early!\n\nCost: Free! \n\nAbout the Bar: This is a no-
 host bar\, so drinks are on your own tab. \n\n\\*\\*\\* The first 50 peopl
 e to RSVP will receive one complimentary drink from Los Cien!\n\nWhat to E
 xpect:\n\nMusic\n\nDelicious appetizers\n\nDecorate-a-puerquito contest\n\
 nKaraoke hosted by DJ Quetzali\n\nFlip cup\n\nAnd more holiday fun!\n\nThi
 s celebration is our way of saying much&iacute\;simas gracias to the volun
 teers\, staff\, members\, and familia who make Los Cien what it is. Bring 
 your holiday spirit and celebrate a year of progress with us. We just want
  to hang out\, celebrate\, and show our gratitude for a community that lif
 ts us all.
LOCATION:Sally Tomatoes
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/loscien-holidayparty-2026?
 aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Muunjuun & Sakoyana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T203000
UID:261127TICsemHtrEagl79yvoXTXg
DESCRIPTION:A cosmic funk dance party in West County: Sakoyana\, Muunjuun
 ’s first full-band show. Plus DJ Bankshot.\n\nCome ready to move.\n\nThr
 ee acts\, one long night of groove at The Forestville Club\, for fans of K
 hruangbin\, Vulfpeck\, Thundercat and Parliament-Funkadelic.\n\nSakoyana i
 s a Sonoma County band that can turn on a dime from tight\, horn-sharp gro
 oves into wide-open jams. Think Snarky Puppy at a backyard party: the kind
  of set that makes the drummer grin and the whole room bounce.\n\nMuunjuun
  MOON-june plays music that feels like tripping without the mushrooms. Boo
 tsy Collins called him a “west coast cosmic funktroid.” This is his fi
 rst show with the full five-piece band\, so expect warm\, wobbly\, sky-hig
 h pop-funk that pulls you onto the floor and keeps you there.\n\nDJ Banksh
 ot keeps the floor moving between sets\, so there’s no reason to sit dow
 n.\n\nFriday\, December 11th · 8:30 PM The Forestville Club · Forestvill
 e\, CA $20 · advance tickets $25 · at the door Limited capacity 21\\+
LOCATION:The Forestville Club
URL:https://www.muunjuun.com/shop/p/sakoyana-muunjuun-live-at-the-forestvi
 lle-club-dec-11
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Native Plant Garden Volunteer Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T120000
UID:261126NzbEl0rp30CCTY1r4zco2Q
DESCRIPTION:Share Your Passion for Pollinators—Join Us in the Garden!\n\
 nJoin the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for a volunteer morning in our 4
 -acre Native Plant Demonstration Garden at the Laguna Environmental Center
 ! Help keep this beautiful garden thriving while connecting with community
  and nature.\n\nVolunteers help with planting\, pruning\, weeding\, and sp
 reading wood chips while caring for a diverse landscape of native wildflow
 ers\, grasses\, trees\, and more. Enjoy special garden features like a liv
 ing willow tunnel\, tranquil pond\, scenic bridge\, and observation deck.\
 n\nNo experience necessary—we provide training\, tools\, and snacks! Wea
 r clothes you don't mind getting dirty. Only heavy rain cancels.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://GardenVolunteerDay1211.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T235900
UID:261124haE8mkBBv06EDmlCIxUeKA
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
