BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stanroy Song Service: Ryan Woodard\, Andrew Maurer\, Lindsey McFar
 land
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T193000
UID:261115uMhnICOYYUKOKY3IguILsw
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird2 at checkout. Offer ends December 6th.\n\nPromo
  Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\,
  but must be typed as one word.\n\nStanroy Music Center Presents Song Serv
 ice\, an intimate evening with three artists passing the spotlight. Expect
  insights into the craft of the song from inspiration to final form.\n\nAt
  20 years old\, Sonoma County singer-songwriter and multi-instrumentalist 
 Ryan Woodard is rapidly establishing himself as a rising star in the music
  industry. Diagnosed with autism at age three\, Ryan found his voice throu
 gh music\, defying expectations after being considered nonverbal until he 
 was nine. His extraordinary journey took a definitive leap forward at age 
 11 when he shared the stage with blues icon Buddy Guy. Since then\, Ryan
 ’s remarkable talent and story have captured international attention\, e
 arning features in Guitar World Magazine and a gifted Martin guitar from J
 ohn Mayer. Known for his dynamic\, high-energy live performances\, Ryan is
  driven by a singular vision: to perform in the world's greatest arenas an
 d take home multiple Grammy Awards.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/ryanwooda
 rdrocks/\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@ryanwoodard\n\nhttps://www.facebook.c
 om/ryanwoodardrocks/\n\nLindsey McFarland is a soulful singer\, songwriter
 \, and acoustic guitarist. She is known for heartfelt performances and uni
 que original songs\, often inspired by the natural beauty of Sonoma County
 . Her singing and guitar arrangements are inspired by generations of femal
 e musicians\, from Joni Mitchell and the Indigo Girls to Phoebe Bridgers\,
  Susan Tedeschi\, and so many more.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/lindseymc
 farlandmusic\n\nAndrew Maurer was raised in Santa Rosa\, California and ha
 s been writing songs and playing instruments for 30 years. Drawing inspira
 tion from US folk traditional music and songwriters such as Kate Wolf\, El
 liot Smith\, or Mississippi John Hurt\, he crafts his own style and regula
 rly plays live at wine bars. His 2025 EP called “When the Sadness Subsid
 es” can be found on all streaming platforms.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.co
 m/maurer.andrew Stanroy Music Center - located at 850 4th Street in Downto
 wn Santa Rosa celebrates it's 76th anniversary this year. A locally owned\
 , full-service music store providing instrument sales and rentals\, privat
 e music lessons\, and repairs. Stanroy Music Center - serving Sonoma Count
 y musicians and their families since 1947. More at www.stanroy.com
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000E5nXtMAJ
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Cuvaison
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T190000
UID:261115ZzUybj52qkiCKtC3o2GM3g
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of the holiday season with Bright Nights\,
  an evening wine tasting experience set against one of Cuvaison’s most e
 nchanting backdrops: rows and rows of estate vineyards illuminated with tw
 inkling lights.\n\nOffered Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunday evenings from No
 vember 27 through January 3\, Bright Nights invites you to experience the 
 beauty of wine country after dark as the vineyard comes alive with a warm 
 holiday glow. From 5:00pm to 7:00pm\, settle in for a cozy seasonal tastin
 g featuring a selection of Cuvaison wines served with seasonal cheese and 
 charcuterie pairing.\n\nWhether you’re gathering with friends\, celebrat
 ing the season\, or creating a new holiday tradition\, Bright Nights offer
 s a festive and memorable way to enjoy the estate.\n\nExperience Highlight
 s:\n\n·         Rows of estate vineyards illuminated with twinkli
 ng holiday lights\n\n·         Curated wine and cheese pairings\n
 \n·         Festive evening tasting from 5:00pm to 7:00pm\n\n· 
         A magical seasonal setting for friends and holiday gatherin
 gs\n\nThis special tasting experience is offered Fridays\, Saturdays and S
 undays from November 27 through January 3\, with reservations beginning at
  5:00\, 5:15\, and 5:30pm. Please include all guests in your reservation.\
 n\nCuvaison and Brandlin Estate members receive preferred pricing and will
  see a $35 discount for up to 4 guests applied at checkout. Please use the
  email address where you receive membership updates in order for your disc
 ount to apply.\n\nCuvaison kindly asks that all guests be 21 years of age 
 or older to enjoy this experience (unless otherwise noted for special fami
 ly friendly dates). The patio is closed during Bright Nights\, so Cuvaison
  is not able to accommodate pets.\n\nImportant Dates:\n\nThursday\, Novemb
 er 12 – Industry Event\n\nSaturday\, November 15 – Member Pick-up Even
 t + Holiday Shopping\n\nFriday\, November 27 – Bright Nights Launch + Bl
 ack Friday Specials\n\nThursday\, December 3 – Bright Nights Workshop ev
 ent\n\nSunday\, December 13 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk 
 + cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also
  include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 27 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk + cookie pairing fo
 r kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also include a photogra
 pher offering Holiday Family portraits.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Estate Tasting Room
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
