BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ornament-Making Workshop at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T163000
UID:261123O3tx66Sct0C2-A-VP-C9Yg
DESCRIPTION:Enter Jack and Charmian London’s world with a hands-on ornam
 ent-making workshop at the House of Happy Walls Museum. Guests will explor
 e turn-of-the-century traditions from a time when decorated trees glowed w
 ith real candles and homes were filled with handmade treasures and small g
 ifts.\n\nParticipants will create their own period-inspired ornaments to t
 ake home while enjoying the cozy and festive atmosphere of the museum.  A
 ll materials are provided\, and everyone will leave with a couple of handm
 ade ornaments to share the holiday cheer.\n\nLight refreshments will be pr
 ovided.  This hands-on workshop is designed with adults in mind and isn
 ’t suitable for young children.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/antique-treasures-ornament-making-wo
 rkshop-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carolynne Marshall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T160000
UID:261123MJHhrTyHpkWH6QZfgHm7Fg
DESCRIPTION:**Class Description:**\n\nAsemic writing is the creation of ma
 rks that resemble handwriting but carry no literal meaning or readable tex
 t. It is the word before words form—the voice too distant to be understo
 od—a universal expression without country or dialect.\n\nWe’ll begin w
 ith a slideshow exploring the rich history and possibilities of asemic wri
 ting\, from ancient scripts and symbols to the calligraphic line and the w
 ork of contemporary artists. From there\, you’ll begin your own explorat
 ion using ink\, watercolor\, and a variety of tools on paper.\n\nThrough g
 uided exercises and playful experimentation\, we’ll explore line\, gestu
 re\, rhythm\, repetition\, and space. You’ll discover how asemic marks c
 an infiltrate and transform your existing artwork or become works of art i
 n their own right.\n\nYou’ll leave with a collection of new work\, fresh
  approaches to mark-making\, and a deeper trust in your own intuition and 
 expressive voice. My intention is to guide you beyond casual scribbling to
 ward authentic marks—marks that arise from the heart and become uniquely
  your own.\n\nAll levels welcome.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classeslectures/p/introductiontoasemicwriting1
 212
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
