BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker with Winemaker Jeff Mangahas of Williams Selyem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T193000
UID:261127tsa4x-yY-E2Rda0vZjPMrw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special evening with Winemaker Jeff Mangahas of 
 Williams Selyem\, one of Sonoma County's most celebrated wineries and a tr
 ue pioneer of Russian River Valley Pinot Noir!\n\nWhat began in a small ga
 rage in 1979 with two friends\, Burt Williams and Ed Selyem\, has grown in
 to one of California's most respected wine brands. Today\, Jeff Mangahas c
 arries on that remarkable legacy\, bringing his background in science\, pa
 ssion for exceptional vineyards\, and thoughtful approach to winemaking to
  every vintage. Jeff's own journey with Williams Selyem began with a singl
 e glass of their Pinot Noir that inspired him to leave his career in resea
 rch and pursue winemaking.\n\nJoin Jeff and our team for an evening of gre
 at wine and conversation as he takes you behind the scenes of Williams Sel
 yem\, sharing the stories\, passion\, and craftsmanship that have shaped o
 ne of Sonoma County’s most celebrated wineries.\n\nYour tasting experien
 ce includes:\n\n- A special selection of four Williams Selyem wines\n\n- D
 eliciously paired food bites\n\n- The opportunity to meet Jeff\, ask quest
 ions\, and hear firsthand about the wines and the winery's incredible hist
 ory\n\nIt's a wonderful opportunity to experience one of Sonoma County's m
 ost iconic wineries in a relaxed\, personal setting at Region. Seating wil
 l be limited for this exclusive event.
LOCATION:Region.
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/regionsonoma/event/630131/meet-the-maker-w
 ith-williams-selyem-winemaker-jeff-mangahas
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T235900
UID:2611247B4pZ72O3k-9FX4ciFa1Pw
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
