BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fr. Brendan Williams - Poems/Prayers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
UID:260819ZkYENL6yxkepTRuprAJImg
DESCRIPTION:Father Brendan Williams\, chaplain of Bishop's Ranch outside H
 ealdsburg\, in conversation with Denise Low. The intersections of prayer a
 nd poetry are shared inspirations from religious traditions for both of th
 ese poets. They will talk about biblical and other religious texts as subl
 iminal cultural guides as well as deliberate choices they make in their re
 spective practices. Psalms and hymns have long influenced sonnets and toda
 y's short lyrical poems. Ginsberg's Kaddish is an audacious example of int
 ertextual borrowing from Jewish tradition. Williams is a priest\, spiritua
 l director\, yogi\, healer\, scholar\, and teacher of religion. His work s
 pans Western and Eastern esoterica\, indigenous Gaelic lifeways\, meditati
 on\, and contemplative spirituality. He chants old rebel tales\, traces th
 e song-streams of ancient wisdom\, and ferries souls along the mythic rive
 rways of human transformation-guiding people from all walks of life back t
 o their birthright of wholeness and freedom within the great ecology of sp
 irit.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/fr-brendan-williams-poems-prayers/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
