BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers General Meeting  w/Korie Leigh: Write the Book You
  Need
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T133000
UID:261127NQLzU8F92keQl1WjgrUNaA
DESCRIPTION:Korie Leigh: Write the Book You Need\n\nDec. 19\, 2026\, 11 a.
 m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa\n\nPlease bring something savory or sweet t
 o share in our potluck!\n\n“Write the Book You Need” is a reflective a
 nd practical workshop for people who feel called to turn lived experience 
 into meaningful writing.\n\nDrawing from her work as an author\, clinician
 \, and educator\, Dr. Korie Leigh explores how personal stories can become
  books that help readers feel seen\, supported\, or less alone. Participan
 ts will learn how to identify the gap their story fills\, move beyond memo
 ir into broader reader impact\, and begin shaping experiences into a book 
 with purpose\, clarity\, and resonance.\n\nAbout the Presenter:\n\nKorie L
 eigh\, PhD\, FT\, CCLS\, is an award-winning author\, thanatologist\, cert
 ified child life specialist\, and Associate Professor and Program Chair of
  Thanatology at Marian University. She has spent more than twenty years su
 pporting seriously ill and dying children and their families across pediat
 ric hospitals\, oncology\, hospice\, palliative care\, and community setti
 ngs.\n\nShe serves as Director of Psychosocial Services and a board member
  at Hero’s Path Pediatric Palliative Care and has served as a childhood 
 grief advisor to Sesame Workshop. She is the author of four traditionally 
 published books with more than 22\,000 copies sold. What Does Grief Feel L
 ike? \\(Free Spirit Publishing\, 2023\\) has sold more than 10\,000 copies
 \, won a New Mexico Book Award\, appeared on Oprah’s recommended reading
  list\, and had international rights purchased by Indonesia’s Ministry o
 f Education. It Won’t Ever Be the Same: A Teen’s Guide to Grief and Gr
 ieving \\(Free Spirit Publishing\, 2024\\) has also sold more than 10\,000
  copies and reached \\#1 on Amazon in the Teen & Young Adult Grief categor
 y.\n\nHer other titles are When Everything Changes: Parenting Through Loss
  and Grief \\(2026\\) and Why Are the Numbers All Jumbled? \\(2026\\). She
  lives in Santa Fe\, NM. Find Korie Leigh at www.korieleighphd.com.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/dec-2026-korie-leigh/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"To Build a Fire\," A Jack London Reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T153000
UID:261127EN2zW9ZJkUu430gAB24U0Q
DESCRIPTION:Gather in the warmth of the House of Happy Walls as Jeff Falco
 ner brings Jack London’s powerful storytelling to life through a live re
 ading of “To Build a Fire.” Experience the suspense\, vivid imagery\, 
 and chilling atmosphere of the Yukon as London’s words unfold. The readi
 ng will be followed by a discussion exploring the story’s themes and its
  lasting significance.  \\(This story addresses difficult topics and the 
 challenges faced in survival situations. The material may be intense and i
 s not recommended for young children.\\)
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/to-build-a-fire/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
