BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T235900
UID:261124F_IaQzSEc0Wf6v3pcQpsfw
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wreath Making Workshop with Wildflower Wreaths x Petaluma Floral
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T120000
UID:261123zRWjgYFK40SOR8ld2pqilg
DESCRIPTION:Boutique Botanical Wreath-Making Workshop | Wildflower Wreaths
  x Petaluma Floral\n\nGet creative and think outside the circle! Join Wild
 flower Wreaths and Petaluma Floral for a hands-on botanical wreath-making 
 workshop.\n\nLearn the basics of wreath construction\, explore color and d
 esign\, and discover techniques to take your creation from traditional to 
 wild. Experiment with a curated assortment of fresh and dried botanicals t
 o create a one-of-a-kind wreath to take home.\n\nAll experience levels are
  welcome! All materials and tools are provided\, along with a holiday beve
 rage of your choice from Caffeine Inc. Just bring your imagination and a w
 illingness to get creative!\n\nA fun way to escape the holiday hustle\, en
 joy some creative time\, and make something beautiful for yourself or some
 one special.\n\nDecember 19 | 10 AM–12 PM Petaluma Floral | Petaluma\, C
 A $175 per person\n\nLimited to 6 participants. Advance registration and p
 ayment required.
LOCATION:Petaluma Floral
URL:https://www.instagram.com/p/DgD2v8USsZb/?lqvp=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Christmas Nightmare with the Renegade Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T200000
UID:261123FchMnDfmsUmg6UZ842At9g
DESCRIPTION:The Renegade Orchestra presents “A Christmas Nightmare” in
  downtown Napa\n\nWhat happens when musicians get tired of playing the sam
 e old holiday songs - the Renegade Orchestra presents a Christmas Nightmar
 e. No more sappy Rudolph’s - this show is all about the darker side of C
 hristmas. \n\nThe bay area’s favorite rock and roll orchestra plays mus
 ic for a not so silent night featuring frostbite and fiddles\, a creepy li
 ttle Christmas\, and carols in the keys of shadows.\n\nSongs include Wizar
 ds in Winter from the Trans-Siberian Orchestra\, a dark medley of Balkan h
 olidays songs\, and\, of course\, a little Danny Elfman from Nightmare bef
 ore Christmas. \n\nThe concert will be held at the beautiful\, but lesser
  known\, Grand Hall of the Native Sons of the Golden West\, right downtown
  on Coombs St. in Napa.
LOCATION:Native Sons of the Golden West
URL:http://RenegadeOrchestra.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
